    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "A single informant in Sikar sent an email with PDFs that matched the chemistry paper perfectly, acting as a leverage point for systemic correction. This communication forced the national agency to cancel the medical entrance exam and refer 26–27 paper setters and translators to the investigation agency, exposing a network of manipulators. The consequence was the arrest of thirteen people, including a coaching figure, and a new examination date scheduled for June 21, resetting a flawed process.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Magician",
        "fragments": [
